          %h3#poisson_lie_group_structure Poisson Lie group structure
          %p
            Under addition a Lie-Poisson manifold becomes a
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+Lie+group"} Poisson Lie group
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              a
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moment+map"} moment map
              is often expresses as a Poisson homomorphism into a Lie-Poisson structure.
          %h2#references References
          %p
            The notion of Lie-Poisson structures was originally found by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sophus+Lie"} Sophus Lie
            and then rediscovered by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Felix+Berezin"} Felix Berezin
            and by
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Kirillov"} Alexander Kirillov
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bertram+Kostant"} Bertram Kostant
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean-Marie+Souriau"} Jean-Marie Souriau
          %p General accounts:
          %ul
            %li#BayenFlatoFronsdalLichnerowiczSternheimer78
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fran%C3%A7ois+Bayen"}> François Bayen
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mosh%C3%A9+Flato"} Moshé Flato
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Christian+Fronsdal"} Christian Fronsdal
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andr%C3%A9+Lichnerowicz"} André Lichnerowicz
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Sternheimer"} Daniel Sternheimer
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Deformation theory and quantization. I. Deformations of symplectic structures.
                %strong 111
                1 (1978) 61-110 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0003-4916(78)90224-5"}> doi:10.1016/0003-4916(78)90224-5
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alan+Weinstein"}> Alan Weinstein
                , §3 in:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The local structure of Poisson manifolds
                %strong 18
                3 (1983) 523-557 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://projecteuclid.org/journals/journal-of-differential-geometry/volume-18/issue-3/The-local-structure-of-Poisson-manifolds/10.4310/jdg/1214437787.full"}> doi:10.4310/jdg/1214437787
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                Izu Vaisman, section 3.1 of
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Lectures on the Geometry of Poisson Manifolds
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Camille+Laurent-Gengoux"}> Camille Laurent-Gengoux
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Linear Poisson Structures and Lie Algebras
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pol+Vanhaecke"} Pol Vanhaecke
                (eds.),
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Poisson Structures
                %strong 347
                179-203 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-642-31090-4_7"}> doi:10.1007/978-3-642-31090-4_7
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p Monograph:
          %ul
            %li#Waldmann07
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stefan+Waldmann"}> Stefan Waldmann
              , pp. 220 in:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Poisson-Geometrie und Deformationsquantisierung
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-540-72518-3"} doi:10.1007/978-3-540-72518-3
          %p
            On the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+deformation+quantization"} formal deformation quantization
            of Lie-Poisson structures via transfer of the product on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+enveloping+algebra"} universal enveloping algebra
            of the given Lie algebra:
          %ul
            %li#Gutt83
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Simone+Gutt"}> Simone Gutt
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  An explicit
                  = succeed "-product" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo *
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ast
              %strong 7
              (1983) 249–258 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BF00400441"}> doi:10.1007/BF00400441
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p reviewed in:
          %ul
            %li#Gutt11
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Simone+Gutt"}> Simone Gutt
              , §2.2 of:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Deformation quantization of Poisson manifolds
              %strong 17
              (2011) 171-220 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://msp.org/gtm/2011/17/p003.xhtml"}> gtm:17
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://msp.org/gtm/2011/17/gtm-2011-17-003p.pdf"} pdf
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0003107"} arXiv:math/0003107
          %p and generalization to more general polynomial Poisson algebras is discussed in
          %ul
            %li
              Michael Penkava, Pol Vanhaecke,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Deformation Quantization of Polynomial Poisson Algebras
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/9804022"} arXiv:math/9804022
          %p
            On
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+deformation+quantization"} strict deformation quantization
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie-Poisson+structures"} Lie-Poisson structures
            via
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+algebras"} group algebras
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marc+A.+Rieffel"}> Marc A. Rieffel
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Lie Group Convolution Algebras as Deformation Quantizations of Linear Poisson Structures
              %strong 112
              4 (1990) 657-685 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.2307/2374874"}> doi:10.2307/2374874
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://www.jstor.org/stable/2374874"} jstor:2374874
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+Lie+groupoid"} symplectic Lie groupoid
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+integration"} Lie integrating
            Lie-Poisson structures is discussed as example 4.3 in:
          %ul
            %li#BursztynCrainic
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Henrique+Bursztyn"}> Henrique Bursztyn
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marius+Crainic"} Marius Crainic
              %em Dirac structures, momentum maps and quasi-Poisson manifolds
              (
              %a{:href => "http://www.preprint.impa.br/FullText/Bursztyn__Fri_Dec_23_11_24_19_BRDT_2005.html/alanfestimpa.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Victor+Ginzburg"}> Victor Ginzburg
